<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Li Te</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 303</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Li Te was a Ba-Di leader who led refugees fleeing famine in the north-west into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sichuan">Sichuan</a> around 298, under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-jin-dynasty">Western Jin dynasty</a>. When Jin officials tried to force the refugees back, he rebelled in 301 and fought the provincial governor Luo Shang around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chengdu">Chengdu</a>, but was killed in 303. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/li-xiong">Li Xiong</a> took Chengdu the next year and founded the Cheng Han state, which later honoured Li Te as an emperor.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/li-te.jpg" alt="Li Te" width="320" height="465" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: see below · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Harvard_drs_49802792_%E7%B9%A1%E5%83%8F%E4%B8%89%E5%9C%8B%E6%BC%94%E7%BE%A9%E7%BA%8C%E7%B7%A8_v.1_(%E6%9D%8E%E7%89%B9).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
